# Real variable values never enter the repository.
#
# `environments/offline-plan.tfvars` IS committed and is deliberately not
# matched here: every value in it is impossible on purpose (account 000000000000,
# region `xx-plan-1`, an RFC 2606 `.invalid` domain) and it exists so CI can run
# the offline plan spec-doc6 §13.3 requires. A reviewer should be able to read
# exactly what the plan was produced from.
#
# `terraform.tfvars` and the `*.auto.tfvars` family are the opposite: they hold
# the account id, region, domain and hosted zone id that §D5 declares as
# variables with no default. Those are the owner's facts about his account, they
# are supplied at apply time, and the runbook in `docs/DEPLOY_AWS.md` says where
# each one comes from.
terraform.tfvars
terraform.tfvars.json
*.auto.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars.json

# Backend wiring for a real state bucket, created by the runbook's first step.
backend.hcl

# Plan output. A saved plan file contains every computed value in the
# configuration, which after an apply includes resolved secret ARNs.
plan.txt
*.tfplan

# Offline plan output. Regenerated by `./infra/plan-offline.sh --artifact` and
# uploaded as a CI artifact; it is derived, not authored.
plan-output/
